      "question": {
        ":question/id": "bfb8dc7a-8efe-5c10-8f98-d40a62827a4c",
        ":question/problem": "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 2 \\cdot 3^{x} \\left(3^{x} + 2\\right)^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nWork where $3^{x} + 2>0$.\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=3^{x} + 2$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(3^{x} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nWork where $3^{x} + 2>0$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 2 \\cdot 3^{x} \\left(3^{x} + 2\\right)^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{2}{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}\\left(\\int u^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int u^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\frac{u^{3}}{3}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}\\left(\\int u^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{2}{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}\\left(\\frac{u^{3}}{3}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 \\left(3^{x} + 2\\right)^{3}}{3 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}+C.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
